        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Plan on about fifteen years from a mini split, with twenty possible when it was installed carefully and cared for. The years you lose usually trace back to a few things: a rushed install, clogged filters and dirty coils, salt air, or electrical surges that take out the inverter board.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When something fails, match the repair to the age and warranty. Fix sensors, fans and leaks freely. Lean on the warranty for boards and compressors. And once an older system out of warranty needs a compressor, put that money toward a new system rather than an old one.
          </p>
